WEBVTT

00:03:28.382 --> 00:03:31.753
Still, the philosophy of cynicism 
had admirers,

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:34.395
especially among those 
who wished to question

00:03:34.395 --> 00:03:35.895
the state of society.

00:03:35.895 --> 00:03:39.402
The 18th-century French philosopher 
Jean-Jacques Rousseau

00:03:39.402 --> 00:03:41.596
was called the “new Diogenes”

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:45.341
when he argued 
that the arts, sciences, and technology,

00:03:45.341 --> 00:03:47.141
corrupt people.

00:03:47.141 --> 00:03:50.762
In 1882, Friedrich Nietzsche 
reimagined a story

00:03:50.762 --> 00:03:54.217
in which Diogenes 
went into the Athenian marketplace

00:03:54.217 --> 00:03:55.277
with a lantern,

00:03:55.277 --> 00:03:58.692
searching in vain 
for a single honest person.

00:03:58.692 --> 00:04:00.286
In Nietszche’s version,